5k9p|n|The third month of the year, containing thirty-one days. ; A territorial border or frontier; a region adjacent to a boundary line; a confine; -- used chiefly in the plural, and in English history applied especially to the border land on the frontiers between England and Scotland, and England and Wales. ; The act of marching; a movement of soldiers from one stopping place to another; military progress; advance of troops. ; Hence: Measured and regular advance or movement, like that of soldiers moving in order; stately or deliberate walk; steady onward movement. ; The distance passed over in marching; as, an hour's march; a march of twenty miles. ; A piece of music designed or fitted to accompany and guide the movement of troops; a piece of music in the march form.	a:37cn,119,39;4g88,97,14;8vzk,93,8;3gnm,80,4;9v22,76,7;3iwv,76,47;4rnr,76,15;a3p4,75,4;37ch,71,1;20wm,70,3;7n1i,63,3;4deh,63,58;9wp9,61,36;aik5,54,2;7vrs,52,3~5dsp,19,410;547d,6,162;2q9v,35,156;54or,38,149;4deh,63,58;3iwv,76,47;5srs,21,46;5tei,35,40;37cn,119,39;9wp9,61,36;37ci,43,30;37by,29,28;9ni2,21,27;2ruy,15,26;6xup,0,25	v:383q,84,6;25zf,76,220;7cwk,74,3;7cci,67,6;7ya,65,17;4db4,64,5;1k9z,59,4;a3p4,55,1;6zls,54,6;3eim,49,177;33q0,48,8;4rnr,47,2;ahxp,46,18;2v95,44,4;6vp3,43,2~25zf,76,220;3eim,49,177;1vn,42,104;7vq8,36,96;9152,11,82;2vso,21,51;a4vo,1,46;7j9p,22,46;80fr,39,45;37by,33,37;7akr,0,33;11s1,28,32;ui2,7,29;2vvw,20,26;5wx3,3,21	V:3z2m,44,4;2yq6,43,4;3j97,33,9;44cw,29,4;5p0o,23,19~5p0o,23,19;3j97,33,9;2yq6,43,4;44cw,29,4;3z2m,44,4	n:37c4,111,4;5x12,99,6;2pth,89,8;9wbi,87,17;37cn,86,4;8vzk,83,4;2fdd,83,12;37ch,81,2;67si,80,9;37ci,79,362;3ge2,75,6;62a7,73,4;14hj,71,6;7vrs,70,11;arp0,69,8~8pj0,22,1085;a4dx,33,603;6ux,11,578;ual,15,489;w46,13,446;37ci,79,362;27ud,49,269;j3w,13,232;9mne,4,191;a4t1,5,163;2pat,7,78;37by,39,57;9ni2,31,56;3h43,47,41;5xmg,40,34	N:a4si,104,1;3z2m,92,113;2yq6,92,121;hhw,78,561;6ywc,72,3;44cw,56,27;20fu,50,23;7j51,45,18;3j97,36,11;4rim,33,27;20cz,30,2;8q37,29,3;8qck,29,1;