5ko0|n|A meeting together of people, at a stated time and place, for the purpose of traffic (as in cattle, provisions, wares, etc.) by private purchase and sale, and not by auction; as, a market is held in the town every week. ; A public place (as an open space in a town) or a large building, where a market is held; a market place or market house; esp., a place where provisions are sold. ; An opportunity for selling anything; demand, as shown by price offered or obtainable; a town, region, or country, where the demand exists; as, to find a market for one's wares; there is no market for woolen cloths in that region; India is a market for English goods. ; Exchange, or purchase and sale; traffic; as, a dull market; a slow market. ; The price for which a thing is sold in a market; market price. Hence: Value; worth. ; The privelege granted to a town of having a public market.	a:6lw8,100,8;4lz5,92,13;2xqv,91,10;2c6r,88,4;tt8,83,17;30yb,82,19;5y3g,81,18;5y3l,79,6;3euz,79,89;8s41,77,3;2p4a,76,5;6lw9,75,6;4brg,75,30;15pr,74,14;1ppe,74,537~d4e,56,7312;3go7,37,2166;218w,21,1515;6nwu,19,1274;35mc,52,1200;ys5,37,1173;8eh5,52,811;9ra8,24,760;2rxg,39,734;8pm3,10,600;1ppe,74,537;3aeh,56,505;5cam,13,473;7b0p,25,356;53yv,8,297	v:8sfq,80,2;2ugs,79,297;41v8,77,4;8b2y,76,5;6nyc,67,2;7dr6,63,66;15zd,59,3;9mle,55,11;11g2,52,12;2pmv,49,3;31wq,46,6;560n,46,7;56u0,45,22;8bxf,45,7;w39,45,40~2ugs,79,297;3voq,27,73;7dr6,63,66;5efz,19,57;7cfl,18,41;w39,45,40;82rz,29,39;35tk,14,34;3joy,30,33;3kb0,28,32;2cq2,26,27;308o,17,24;52v9,36,23;56u0,45,22;6ju8,3,21	V:2mit,85,11;1xt0,77,3;997h,76,6;90h0,73,4;9ebo,71,16;77lj,69,5;7p48,66,9;1vic,64,17;1215,64,6;2ypf,62,2;18sn,62,12;77mk,60,3;ewy,57,8;7s0a,56,5;80td,55,1~5ije,18,664;3sf5,15,378;5zpe,28,236;4dmj,42,226;6oac,29,165;9lpb,32,144;1k3l,38,141;2nwf,30,98;1l5y,35,97;33j2,28,93;8g7h,23,92;7nzu,13,89;aieh,3,82;58qn,39,73;xcs,39,66	n:6nyc,116,57;3cd2,98,301;4q9b,97,4;58dn,94,371;8lda,93,6;4k3a,91,54;6r0h,85,112;t8e,84,3;3euz,84,125;93dg,81,7914;8sfq,80,2